  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post arrival Reception Assistance to Returnees from Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia is consistently mired in protracted conflict and cyclical disasters related to hazards that cause displacement and increased vulnerabilities to mobile populations. Migrants traveling along the Eastern Corridor to Yemen and Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) continue to increase particularly Somali and Ethiopian nationals. With respect to the mandate and specialized support of each agency, IOM and UNHCR continue to support Somalis to voluntarily return home under the Assisted Spontaneous Return (ASR) arrangement from July 2023 to December 2023. UNHCR is taking the lead on the identification, pre-screening, pre-and return forms of assistance and boat arrangements from Aden, Yemen to Berbera, Somaliland, while IOM is engaging in this program to provide pre-return support, Onward Transportation Assistance (OTA), and post-arrival support in the Port of Entry (PoE) in Berbera, Somaliland.</narrative>
  </description>
